abstract: >
  We present the Unitary Manifold (UM), a five-dimensional Kaluza-Klein
  framework in which thermodynamic irreversibility, information flow, and
  quantum transition asymmetry are unified as projections of a single
  higher-dimensional geometry. Dimensional reduction of the 5D
  Einstein-Hilbert action yields a 4D effective action whose field equations —
  the Walker-Pearson equations — show that the Second Law of Thermodynamics is
  a geometric identity rather than a statistical postulate. As of v34.0
  (2026-09-02), the hardgated core comprises 208 pillars and the repository
  tracks 992 total pillar slots, with next slot 993. Full regression stands at
  62,525 passed · 48 skipped · 12 deselected · 0 failed, and the Lean4 corpus
  stands at 3,912 theorems. Sprint BL consolidates the surviving flavor-family
  residuals into one explicit UV flavor/moduli boundary and wires PDG/FLAG α_s
  releases into the UV rerun path without inflating closure claims. The framework is internally self-consistent at the
  repository level; external empirical confirmation remains pending. Adjacent
  research tracks (Pillars 218–232+) extend the geometric machinery to quantum
  computing, energy systems, biomedical applications, and AI/robotics as honest
  quantitative explorations, not hardgated physics claims. The primary falsifier
  is the LiteBIRD CMB polarisation birefringence measurement β ∈ {0.273°,
  0.331°} (~2032).
